Macrocells
       An architecture rich in programmable I/O macrocells allows
       integration of a wide range of logic functions. Users can flexibly
       choose the balance of how many inputs and outputs are needed for the
       design. The two MACH subfamilies allow users to choose a device based
       on logic to pin ratios suited to the users needs, but not pay for
       resources that aren't used.
       
       The macrocell has logic resources for implementing 2 types of
       flip-flops, plus combinatorial transfer. All types of registers (SR,
       JK, etc.) can be modeled efficiently via software-generated logic
       emulation. Counters, state machines, and data-path logic can be
       easily integrated.



