Signal Routing
       A single global routing resource for all signal sources  communicates
       all signals equally well to where they are needed. The routing
       software is thus simplified because all paths have equivalent access
       and identical delays. No fancy decision strategies have to account
       for these complications present on other PLD's.
       
       Independent access to both internal logic nodes and pin  sources
       provide additional logic configurations (registered logic with pin
       feedback), plus simultaneous use of a cell as both a buried node and
       device input.





