Clocking and S/R
       Selection of clock sources and banking of Set / Reset / Output
       Enable resources are configured to support synchronous design
       methodologies. The additional overhead of independent FF controls is
       not justified for a general purpose logic family. Such specialization
       will come in later devices.

MACH 2 Family
       Besides the choice of differing logic to pin ratios, the MACH 2
       family multiplies the options for upward migration as designs evolve.
       Up to 16-in OR's can be handled by a larger PT allocator. Additional
       signal routing paths exist to cover high complexity designs which may
       fail in a MACH 1 family device. Each smaller device will be
       "shadowed" by a big brother in the same pinout.

