Additional Banks
       The additional logic banks of the MACH 2 family allow more options on
       which registers are affected by initialization conditions. Each bank
       has a separate term, independent of the ones driving other registers.
       The user can easily have a group of registered logic which is never
       reset or operates on different control signals from the rest of his
       logic.

Input Storage
       The improved setup time for the input storage functions (register and
       latch) allows the system designer to alter the basic interval the
       logic has for resolving its decisions. Additional time is "shifted"
       from before, to after the register. Choice of clock source allows
       special usage, such as retaining input data for later logic
       decisions.


